x=394
y=129
width=48
height=48
layer=com_2
graphic="bank_tabs,1"
clickmask=no

// 767:43
[com_43]
type=graphic
x=401
y=143
width=36
height=32
layer=com_2
graphic="bank_misc_graphics,1"
clickmask=no

// 767:44
[com_44]
type=text
x=12
y=5
width=436
height=82
layer=com_3
textfont=p11_full
text=Using this tab system will allow you to easily group together related items as you wish. For instance, you could place all of your food in one tab, or all of your weapons in another. Alternatively, you could create a tab to contain all of those items you use to train a skill or play a certain activity. There is no limit to the number of times you can rearrange your bank, so feel free to experiment. 
textlineheight=12
textshadow=yes
colour=0xffffff

// 767:45
[com_45]
type=text
x=3
y=96
width=293
height=29
xmode=abs_right
layer=com_3
textfont=p11_full
text=Near the bottom-left corner of the bank you will see a set of four numbers, as shown to the left.
textlineheight=12
textshadow=yes
colour=0xffffff

// 767:46
[com_46]
type=layer
x=38
y=97
width=90
height=25
layer=com_3
op10=  

// 767:47
[com_47]
type=text
x=12
y=137
width=436
height=66
layer=com_3
textfont=p11_full
text=The first two numbers, separated by a diagonal line, represent your non-member bank space and how much of that bank space you have filled with non-member items. The second two numbers, separated by the other diagonal line, represent the bank space you have gained by being a member, and how much of that bank space you have filled with member items.
textlineheight=12
textshadow=yes
colour=0xffffff
op10= 

